WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Drop beetroot cylinders into cold
water and leave them for 30 minutes.

2
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.240
The water stays almost clear.

3
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.850
Repeat it with hot water: this
time the water turns deep red.

4
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.320
Plot results like these
against temperature,

5
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:20.110
and the line creeps up slowly, then shoots
up between 40 and 60 degrees Celsius.

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.520
So why does beetroot bleed its
red pigment into hot water,

7
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.430
but not into cold?

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.260
In this mission, you'll
measure how red the water is,

9
00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.980
using a colorimeter.

10
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:34.890
Then you'll make a dilution series and
turn each reading into a concentration.

11
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.100
Your mission: explain why beetroot bleeds
its red pigment into hot water but not

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:40.910
into cold.
